      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay cool, i'll try the water. but the sting is still really intense and the skin feels super hot... my grandma always says that putting a thick layer of butter or even some heavy oil helps soothe the burn and keeps the air from hitting it which makes it hurt less. if i use a really thick layer of something like coconut oil or butter, wouldn't that actually be better for the pain than just leaving it exposed? it's way more soothing than the water.",
