      "content": "While your grandma's advice has merit, applying a thick layer of coconut oil or butter can actually hinder the healing process by trapping bacteria and moisture, potentially leading to infection. Additionally, butter and oil may create a cooling effect temporarily, but this can be a temporary fix and not a substitute for proper wound care. The initial run of cool water was intended to help combat the heat and reduce the pain, but if the burn is severe, you can also try applying a thin layer of a topical anesthetic like lidocaine or benzocaine after the initial flush.",
